# Per-project route files stay on the box and out of this public repo.
#
# Traefik watches this whole directory, so a project can drop its own routes in
# here - often generated by that project's tooling - and they take effect at
# once. Those files name private work and change without this repo knowing, so
# the default is: NOT tracked.
#
# Deny everything, then allow back the files that genuinely belong to the stack.
# A new project file is therefore ignored automatically, which is the safe way
# round: forgetting to add an ignore rule cannot leak anything.
*
!.gitignore
!auth.yml
!host-services.yml
!portal-api.yml
!project.example.yml
# The file-explorer routes. Stack-owned and load-bearing: it carries the two role
# gates (sso-viewer / sso-editor) that are the ONLY thing standing between the
# tailnet and write access to the repos. It contains no credential - the role
# name is not a secret - and losing it would silently unprotect the write tier,
# so it is tracked. It was ignored by the `*` above for its first two commits,
# which is exactly the failure mode this comment exists to prevent repeating.
!portal-files.yml
# The config-tier routes, tracked for exactly the reason portal-files.yml is:
# they carry the `editor` gate on a service that can rewrite this repo's compose
# files, so losing the file would silently unprotect a write path. It holds no
# credential. Added in the same commit as the file, on the strength of the note
# above - portal-files.yml went two commits untracked before anyone noticed.
!bothy-config.yml
# The redacted twin of the GENERATED portal-prom.yml (which stays ignored by the
# `*` above - it carries a basic-auth credential). Comments only: a live example
# in this directory overwrites the real router, see the file's own header.
!portal-prom.example.yml
